    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "alt", verbatim: "Viktor Kaplan (1876 – 1934) was an Austrian engineer and the inventor of the Kaplan turbine, a revolutionary water turbine used to produce electricity from large streams with only a moderate incline.", marks: 5, accepts: ["James Watt (1736 – 1819) was a Scottish inventor, mechanical engineer whose improvements in steam engine technology drove the Industrial Revolution. To describe the efficiency of his engines, he coined the term 'horsepower' and devised a rev counter.","Gaston Plamté (1834 – 1889) was a French physicist who invented the lead–acid battery. This type of battery was developed as the first rechargeable electric battery marketed for commercial use and it is widely used in automobiles."] },
    ],
